<title>USA: Fed's Phillips promotes review of circuit breakers.</title>
<headline>Fed's Phillips promotes review of circuit breakers.</headline>
<dateline>NASHVILLE, Tenn. 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Reserve Board Governor Susan Phillips said U.S. stock market circuit breakers need to be reviewed periodically to make sure interruptions to trading only occur when market conditions warrant.</p>
<p>Speaking at a Vanderbilt University conference here, Phillips said: &quot;I'm certainly supportive of this kind of review, and think that a periodic evaluation of circuit breakers is valuable to ensure that trading halts only occur during very unusual market conditions.&quot;</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660</p>
